    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0407" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/316: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-11T18:00:00+09:00">January 11, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 12—2:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Special <hi rendition="#italic">Yomiuri</hi> despatch [from] Shanghai states
                    remaining 3,000 American citizens Shanghai expected evacuate near future.
                    Consulate General reportedly recently again advised Americans withdraw. American
                    ships said declining accept reservations non-Americans.</p>
                <p>Sent Department via Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
